{
  "_doc": [
    "World Ablaze constants registry - read by tools/check_constants.py.",
    "HOI4 `@` constants are FILE-SCOPED, so the same quantity is declared in several files, mirrored from",
    "engine defines / building data, and copied into the savegame-analysis tables. Each `group` below is",
    "one such must-match contract: `owner` is the authoritative declaration, every `mirrors` entry must",
    "carry the same value. `governs` says what the number does, so a future reader knows what breaks",
    "when the copies disagree.",
    "Member kinds: pdx_const {file,name} = `@NAME = v` | pdx_global {file,name} = `set_variable = { global.NAME = v }`",
    "| pdx_block_key {file,block,key} = `block = { key = v }` (dotted key walks sub-blocks) | lua_define {file,name}",
    "| py_assign {file,name} | py_literal_has {file,name,value} (dict key / sequence item / tuple-item[0] present)",
    "| regex {file,pattern} (all group-1 captures must agree).",
    "policy: strict (default, ERROR on drift) | advisory (INFO on drift - conventionally equal, may diverge on purpose).",
    "independent_paths: files whose @ names collide with other files by coincidence (per-country MIO data), never a contract.",
    "dead_allowlist: declarations that are intentionally unread in their file (state the reason)."
  ],
  "scan_roots": [
    "common",
    "events"
  ],
  "independent_paths": [
    "common/military_industrial_organization/*"
  ],
  "dead_allowlist": [],
  "groups": [
    {
      "id": "pc_alloc_fraction",
      "governs": "share of the reconstructed civ pool WA_AI_PC_assign_factories may fund per pass; the floored civ gates WA_AI_PC_has_project_civs_16/_20/_31 must judge at the SAME fraction or they refuse projects the fill would pay for (Fix 90; the affordability gate WA_AI_PC_can_afford_project that also read it was deleted by Fix 90b)",
      "owner": {
        "kind": "script_constant",
        "path": "wa_ai_pc.alloc.fraction",
        "file": "common/script_constants/wa_ai_pc.txt"
      },
      "mirrors": [
        {
          "file": ".claude/skills/wa-savegame-analysis/scripts/savegame.py",
          "kind": "py_assign",
          "name": "_PC_ALLOC_FRACTION"
        }
